# REGRESSION (was todo/t0840): the RECEIVER/ROOT-SHAPE axis — the collection
# is not always a bare local. A struct FIELD holding the vector reaches the
# consuming position through a different root, and died the same way pre-fix
# (rc 139, both backends).
#
# ⚠ Two more roots were probed and are deliberately NOT here, each a recorded
# gap rather than a dodge:
#
#   • NESTED container — `outer.push(inner.clone())` where `inner` is a
#     `Vector[Shared[int]]`. `gorget_array_clone` memcpys the elements and
#     consults `elem_clone` for the deep-clone types; a refcount element has no
#     `clone_inplace_fn`, so the two arrays alias the same handles with no
#     incref and both drop (`AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free` in
#     `gorget_shared_drop` under two nested `gorget_array_free` frames). The
#     identical shape with `String` elements is clean. Ships as
#     `shared_nested_vector_clone_over_release.gg` (todo/t0907).
#
#   • FUNCTION RETURN — `Vector[Shared[int]] build(Shared[int] s)`. This one
#     fails on the PARAMETER, not the return: the callee drops its own bare
#     `Shared` param (`todo/t0108` repro (a)/(b), `needs_param_drop`). Drop the
#     parameter and build the handle inside the function and the same shape is
#     ASan-clean, which is what isolates it. The Channel costume ships as
#     `channel_bare_param_callee_drop_uaf.gg`.
#
# CELL: container=Vector · handle=Shared · payload=int · root=struct field.

struct Bag:
    Vector[Shared[int]] items

void main():
    Shared[int] s = Shared[int](6)
    Vector[Shared[int]] empty = []
    Bag b = Bag(empty)
    b.items.push(s.clone())
    b.items.push(s.clone())
    print(f"{b.items.len()}")
    print(f"{b.items.get(0).unwrap().get()}")
    print(f"{s.strong_count()}")
